# BigFred OS — USB LocoNet COM on multi-VCP command stations (stubs).
#
# Digikeijs DR5000 and YaMoRC YD7010 expose three FTDI virtual COM ports
# (LocoNet / XpressNet / config). Symlink ONLY the LocoNet interface after
# measuring on real hardware:
#
#   udevadm info -a -n /dev/ttyUSB0 | grep -E 'idVendor|idProduct|bInterfaceNumber'
#
# Example (fill in real IDs — do not guess multi-interface FTDI):
#
# SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="XXXX", ATTRS{idProduct}=="YYYY", \
#   ATTRS{bInterfaceNumber}=="00", SYMLINK+="loconet-dr5000", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660"
#
# SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="XXXX", ATTRS{idProduct}=="YYYY", \
#   ATTRS{bInterfaceNumber}=="00", SYMLINK+="loconet-yd7010", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660"
#
# Until filled in, use serial:///dev/ttyUSBn:57600 (LocoNet COM from DR5000 Tool /
# YaMoRC docs) and keep knownSerialSymlinks commented for these names in Go.
#
# RB1110 USB-C 28e9:018a is Lenz LI100F — do NOT symlink as loconet-*; use z21 UDP.
